{"name":"Coco","hex":"#d1bba1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Coco","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["An unincorporated community in Kanawha County, West Virginia, United States.","A female given name."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Coco"}],"entries":[{"title":"Coco (2009 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Coco is a 2009 French comedy film written, directed, and starring Gad Elmaleh. The film is based on a character sketch he created for his one-man show \"La Vie Normale\". The film earned $8.5 million in its opening weekend at the French box office, and went on to gross $11.7 million in the European market. Although it was a box office success, Coco was not well received by critics. It received only one star out of four from Première, Paris Match, and Télérama, and two stars from Elle and Le Journal du Dimanche."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/08/Coco_%282009_film%29_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coco_(2009_film)"},{"title":"Coco (2017 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Coco is a 2017 American animated fantasy film directed by Lee Unkrich, and written by Adrian Molina and Matthew Aldrich. Produced by Pixar Animation Studios for Walt Disney Pictures, the film stars the voices of Anthony Gonzalez, Gael García Bernal, Benjamin Bratt, Alanna Ubach, Renée Victor, Ana Ofelia Murguía and Edward James Olmos. It follows a 12-year-old boy in Mexico named Miguel (Gonzalez) who is accidentally transported to the Land of the Dead, where he seeks the help of his deceased musician great-great-grandfather to return him to his family and reverse their ban on music."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/98/Coco_%282017_film%29_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coco_(2017_film)"},{"title":"Coco (franchise)","blocks":[{"text":"Coco is an American media franchise created by Lee Unkrich, Jason Katz, Matthew Aldrich and Adrian Molina. The series takes place in Mexico around the holiday Dia de Muertos and follows Miguel Rivera and his family, the former of whom discovers a link between the living and the dead. The franchise is produced by Pixar Animation Studios and distributed by its parent company Walt Disney Studios Motion Pictures. It began with the 2017 film of the same name, and will be followed by Coco 2 (2029). The franchise also includes three short films, several video games, and a future theme park ride."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Disney%27s_Coco_logo.png/330px-Disney%27s_Coco_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coco_(franchise)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/05/Lee_Unkrich_cropped_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/05/Lee_Unkrich_cropped_2009.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Lee Unkrich (pictured in 2009) first conceptualized Coco in 2010.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALee_Unkrich_cropped_2009.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Adrian_Molina_2017.jpg/500px-Adrian_Molina_2017.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Adrian_Molina_2017.jpg/500px-Adrian_Molina_2017.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Adrian Molina at the 2017 Annecy International Animation Festival","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAdrian_Molina_2017.jpg"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Grey-breasted mountain toucan (Andigena hypoglauca) Caldas","image":"https:/